    "value": "Here are the relevant findings from the OpenTripPlanner GitHub repository regarding \"GBFS\" and \"timezone\":\n\n1. **Timezone Handling in GBFS Integration**\n   - There was a reported issue where the GBFS updater in OTP could not properly retrieve the timezone from certain feeds, resulting in a `NullPointerException`. This happens when `getTimezone()` returns null in the system_information endpoint, which is required by the GBFS specification.\n   - According to the official GBFS JSON schema, the timezone field is a required string in v1.0/v1.1 and is restricted to IANA timezones from v2.0 onward. The OTP updater expects this field to be present; if missing or null, it causes errors when polling GBFS feeds.\n   - The report specifically mentioned that the Bixi Montréal feed was correctly validated (with a valid timezone), while others had unrelated errors but not with the timezone【3:3†source】【3:1†source】.\n\n2. **Configuration and Use of Timezones in OTP**\n   - For OTP graph building and configuration, timezones are critical. The transit model uses a specified timezone (`transitModelTimeZone`), which affects the interpretation of timetables and times in incoming requests. Getting the wrong timezone may shift schedules by a day but is otherwise limited in consequence; still, proper configuration is recommended【3:2†source】.\n\n3. **Changelog Note**\n   - OTP 2.6.0 and later explicitly mention supporting GBFS 2.2, which includes more precise schema checks like required timezones and canonical IANA timezone string values in system information feeds【3:0†source】.\n\n**Summary**: \n- OTP integrates with GBFS feeds and expects the `timezone` field in the `system_information` endpoint, defined as a valid IANA timezone string in recent GBFS versions.\n- If this field is absent or null, OTP updaters may fail with a NullPointerException.\n- Properly validated GBFS feeds (like Bixi Montréal) include this field and pass OTP validation, while those missing it cause updater errors.\n\nFor more in-depth details, see specific issues such as [#6181](https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/6181) and review the [system_information schema](https://github.com/NABSA/gbfs/blob/master/gbfs.md#system_informationjson) in the GBFS specification【3:3†source】.",
